  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA is the dominant signal (rna_only pca_n2000: 0.5907 vs image_only: ~0.33), and the best config so far (config_033: multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat = 0.6186) uses a simple PCA encoder for RNA. We have zero evidence on whether a learned RNA encoder (scgpt or scvi_n200) can improve on PCA. Question: config_005 (scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is a clean single-variable swap of only the RNA encoder relative to config_033, isolating the effect of representation learning vs. linear dimensionality reduction on the dominant modality. Why this is best: Since RNA accounts for most of the predictive signal, the RNA encoder choice is the highest-leverage unexplored axis. A single-variable comparison against our current best (config_033) maximizes information per experiment and directly informs whether investment in learned encoders is warranted before exploring fusion or image-encoder variations."
}

